    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i'm looking at this house in seattle and the contract keeps mentioning \"escrow\" and an \"escrow agent\"... i'm a bit confused. what actually happens with the money while we're waiting to close? like who is holding it and why?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In an escrow, a neutral third-party holds and manages funds until certain conditions are met, in this case, the sale of the house. The escrow agent, typically a title company, receives the earnest money deposit from the buyer and adds it to the escrow account. The agent then sets aside a portion for the seller's portion of the real estate taxes and other closing costs. The escrow agent releases the funds to the seller and/or other parties involved when the sale conditions are fulfilled, such as final inspection and loan approval. This ensures transparency and protects the interests of both parties.",
      "source": "target",
