      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow agents use accounting software and procedures to monitor transactions, keep track of funds, and prevent errors. They also regularly audit and reconcile accounts, and often have internal controls in place to prevent unauthorized access or transactions. Furthermore, escrow agents often have established protocols for handling unusual circumstances, such as a last-minute dispute or a change in the sale terms.",
      "source": "target",
